 "help.intro": "Every word this module's exercises use, on one deck of flashcards: 304 cards, 114 of them nouns. The vocabulary of this module is the words for travel, health, home and describing people, and many verbs you now use in the Perfekt, from the themes Wohnen & Einrichtung, Körper & Gesundheit; beim Arzt, Kleidung & Einkaufen, Menschen beschreiben. Write the German, choose it from four options, or flip the card and rate yourself. A word you miss comes back later in the same run, and stays in your weak words until you get it right three times in a row.",
 "help.tips[0].title": "Learn verbs with their partner",
 "help.tips[0].text": "A verb is only half learnt without the preposition or case it takes. When the back of the card shows a note in brackets, read it aloud with the verb.",
 "help.tips[0].examples[0].en": "to be glad; look forward to / be pleased about",
 "help.tips[0].examples[1].en": "to do, make",
 "help.tips[0].check.q": "A card shows: warten (auf + Akk). Which sentence is correct?",
 "help.tips[0].check.why": "warten needs its partner auf + accusative: auf meinen Freund.",
 "help.tips[0].visual.left": "noun",
 "help.tips[0].visual.right": "its verb",
 "help.tips[0].visual.rows[3].a": "Kleidung",
 "help.tips[1].title": "Putting verbs and position verbs are pairs",
 "help.tips[1].text": "legen / liegen, stellen / stehen, setzen / sitzen, hängen / hängen. The first of each pair moves something (Akkusativ); the second says where it is (Dativ).",
 "help.tips[1].examples[0].en": "I put the book on the table.",
 "help.tips[1].examples[1].en": "The book is on the table.",
 "help.tips[1].check.q": "Die Flasche ____ im Kühlschrank.",
 "help.tips[1].check.why": "The bottle is already there, upright: stehen, with the dative im.",
 "help.tips[2].title": "Reflexive verbs: learn sich with them",
 "help.tips[2].text": "sich freuen, sich treffen, sich beeilen, sich ausruhen: the sich belongs to the verb. Say the whole thing, sich included, every time you learn one.",
 "help.tips[2].examples[0].en": "I'm looking forward to the weekend.",
 "help.tips[2].examples[1].en": "We're meeting at eight.",
 "help.tips[2].check.q": "Beeil ____! Der Bus kommt.",
 "help.tips[2].check.why": "sich beeilen: to a friend the reflexive pronoun is dich.",
 "help.remember[0]": "Never say a noun without its article, not even in your head.",
 "help.remember[1]": "Miss a word? It comes back in the same run. Three correct answers in a row take it off the weak list.",
 "help.remember[2]": "Verbs and adjectives have no article: type them as they stand, like \"an\".",
